                Narrator - Chapter 14 - You are judged for what you were... and punished for not becoming what you’re supposed to be.:
            ► COMPLETED:
                Tess - Look at this. A whole city built on a binary choice. Memory or Reputation.:
                Tess - It's the oldest con in the book - limit the options to control the outcome.:
                Sam - The system is designed to enforce self-policing. They're not just choosing a mask; they're choosing a cage.:
                Sam - The real power isn't in the masks, but in the act of choosing one.:
                Tess - Exactly! And everyone's so committed to the performance. I wonder who's selling the tickets to this show.:
                Kaera - You see this as a performance? These people seem trapped.:
                Tess - Of course it's a performance! The best traps always are. They make you think you're choosing your own identity, but the house always wins.:
                Sam - The woman over there—Ravel. She's the only variable not accounted for in the system. She's not playing.:
                Sam - That makes her either a threat or an opportunity. We should start with her.:
                Moxie - (Grinning) Finally, someone speaking my language. Let's go poke the system.:                
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - tess ("This whole city is a rigged game. I love it. Let's find out who's dealing."):
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - sam ("The binary choice is a fallacy. The true power lies with those who set the terms. We need to find them."):
                EVENT - award_task - meet_ravel

        TASK - Meet Ravel - NPC:
            ► ACQUIRED:
                (no acquired events):
            ► COMPLETED:
                Ravel - ...You're not from here. Your eyes aren't split down the middle.:
                Ravel - This city wants you to choose - Red for Memory, Blue for Reputation. Both are prisons.:
                Kaera - (gently) Forcing people to pick a side like this… it breaks something inside them.:
                Moxie - (grinning) Classic false dichotomy. Create two bad options, make everyone fight over which cage feels better.:
                Kade - (arms crossed) And the ones who refuse to choose become the enemy. Efficient social control.:
                Ravel - (A flicker of respect in her eyes) You see it. Most don't. They're too afraid of being left out.:
                Ravel - I tried wearing both masks. Nearly lost myself. Now I wear nothing... and they hate me for it.:
                Kaera - It takes strength to stand whole when the world demands you fracture.:
                Lyren - (softly) Everything broken still carries pieces of what it was meant to be… You don’t have to choose their broken version of you.:
                Ravel - (Looking toward the armor shop) Hask, the enforcer, watches me. He calls me an error.:
                Ravel - He says a new leader is coming to 'cleanse' the city. Stigma.:
                Tess - (A sharp, dangerous grin) "Cleanse." That's a fun word for a hostile takeover.:
                Tess - So, Stigma creates the problem, lets it fester, and then rides in as the savior. It's a beautiful grift. I almost respect it.:
                Thorn - (low growl) Sounds like another predator wearing a savior’s skin.:
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - ravel ("Hask thinks order is about appearances. He's wrong. It's about being whole."):
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - sam ("Ravel's refusal to choose is a threat to the system. She's a wild card that could disrupt everything."):
                EVENT = set_npc_standing_text - tess ("Ravel's not playing by the rules. She's a wildcard. I like her."):
