        TASK - Meet Caius in Tidekin - NPC:
            ► ACQUIRED:
                (no acquired events):
            ► COMPLETED:
                Caius - You're the ones she sent. Stigma's new favorites.:
                Caius - I can see it in your eyes... that hopeful little spark she gives everyone.:
                Caius - You've seen this place. You've breathed the air. That's all she wanted.:
                Caius - Now go back. Tell her what you saw. Tell her the system is perfect.:                
                Moxie - Perfect? This place is a high-strung nightmare. Everyone's smiling like their face is stapled in place.:
                Caius - (leaning in closer, whispering urgently) Exactly. And Stigma wants to "fix" it by burning it all down and replacing it with her own version.:
                Caius - Edict is cold, controlling, and obsessed with order... but at least his rules are clear.:
                Caius - Stigma? She gets inside your head. She makes you believe you're broken unless you belong to her 'family.' She's not saving anyone. She's collecting them.:                
                Kaera - (frowning) You're saying she's no better than Edict?:
                Caius - (shaking his head) She's worse. Edict demands performance. Stigma demands your soul.:
                Caius - She'll smile while she rewrites who you are. I've seen what happens to people who fully drink her poison... they stop being people.:                
                Kade - (coldly) So we've been played.:
                Chock - (grunting) Great. Another manipulator pretending to be the solution.:
                Poise - Then the real question is, which poison do we choose... or do we burn both?:                
                Caius - (whispering) Just get out while you still can. Tell her whatever she wants to hear.:
                Caius - Before Edict realizes you're here... and before Stigma decides you're too useful to let go.:                
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - caius ("Go back to Stigma. Tell her you understand. Before Edict understands you're here."):
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - jett ("Word travels fast. You went to Tidekin Cove... came back looking like you saw something ugly. Stigma’s ‘family’ isn’t sounding so friendly anymore, is it?"):
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - elian ("You returned from Tidekin Cove quieter than when you left. Whatever you saw there has shaken your faith in Stigma’s promises."):
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - ravel ("Your faces say you didn’t like what you found. Maybe you’re starting to see through her."):
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - hask ("You've returned from Tidekin Cove. If You saw the rot there and still stand with Stigma, then You are truly ready for the cleansing."):
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - sam ("Something in You eyes changed. I don’t trust Stigma’s smile anymore."):
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - tess ("You just got back from Tidekin Cove... You look like You saw behind the curtain. I still want to believe Stigma can fix things... but I’m starting to wonder."):
                EVENT - award_task - return_to_stigma

        TASK - Return to Stigma - NPC:
            ► ACQUIRED:
                (no acquired events):
            ► COMPLETED:
                Stigma - (eyes lighting up) You’re back. And you have the stink of Edict’s city on you. Good. Tell me what did you see?:
                Stigma - The forced smiles? The hollow performances? That is the enemy. Not just Edict, but the very idea of him.:                
                Kaera - (voice heavy) We saw fear wearing a mask of perfection. But we also saw something else.:
                Kade - (cold, direct) We saw another manipulator. One who smiles while she rewrites people from the inside.:
                Moxie - (no longer grinning) You talk about freedom and family, but everything you do is about control. You just hide it better than he does.:                
                Stigma - Control? I offer belonging. I offer healing.:
                Stigma - I offer a place where you don’t have to choose between painful memory and empty performance.:
                Stigma - You felt it in Tidekin Cove, didn’t you? The suffocating weight of expectation. I can free you from all of that.:                
                Chock - By making us choose *you* instead? By turning us into another one of your perfect little masks?:
                Poise - You prey on people’s fear of being incomplete. That’s not salvation. That’s predation.:
                Lyren - You speak of family... but families don’t demand you erase parts of yourself to belong.:                
                Stigma - (her warm smile finally cracks, revealing something colder underneath):
                Stigma - So that’s how it is.:
                Stigma - Even after everything... you still cling to your broken little selves.:
                Stigma - (voice shifting, now laced with venom):
                Stigma - Then I was wrong about you. You’re not ready to be saved.:
                Stigma - You’re just more garbage waiting to be thrown away.:                
                Kade - We’re done being your tools.:
                Chock - Time to end this.:
                EVENT - award_task - defeat_stigma_in_tidekin

        TASK - defeat_stigma_in_tidekin - MOB:
            ► ACQUIRED:
                EVENT - begin_combat - stigma_boss_battle_1 (boss_battle):
            ► COMPLETED:
                Narrator - Stigma’s form flickers and shatters under the final blow. The warm, magnetic aura she projected collapses into something cold and hollow.:
                Narrator - For a moment, her true face is visible — desperate, furious, and deeply afraid.:
                Narrator - Then her body fractures like glass, dissolving into threads of pink and violet light that scatter into the wind.:                
                Stigma - (gasping, voice breaking) You... fools... I was trying to save you from becoming nothing...:
                Stigma - (laughing bitterly as her form unravels) Fine. Run back to Edict and his cold little kingdom of rules. See how long that lasts.:
                Stigma - (voice fading into an echo) You’ll come crawling back... when the masks start to feel comfortable again...:                
                Narrator - The last traces of Stigma’s presence vanish. The air feels suddenly heavier, as if a false warmth has been stripped away, leaving only raw truth behind.:                
                Kaera - She wasn’t saving anyone. She was collecting broken people... and making them more broken. Turning their pain into chains she could hold.:
                Kaera - I wanted to believe someone could offer real belonging in all this chaos... but not like that.:                
                Moxie - Cult leaders are always the same. They just dress it up nicer. “Join my family.” “Let me fix you.” Same poison, prettier bottle.:
                Moxie - At least now we know what she really was — a pretty parasite.:                
                Kade - We’ve been played from the start. She created the division, then positioned herself as the only solution. Classic controlled opposition.:
                Kade - Edict might be a tyrant, but at least his control is honest. Stigma wanted to own who we are.:                
                Chock - (cracking his knuckles, voice low and angry) Talking about unity while trying to erase everything that makes someone themselves...:
                Chock - Yeah. I’ve had enough of her “family.”:
                Chock - Time to find the bastard in the Citadel. Let’s see if he’s any better.:                
                Poise - (quiet, steady) She fed on fear of being incomplete. That kind of hunger doesn’t die easily.:
                Poise - Even if she escaped, her ideas may still linger here.:                
                Lyren - Everything she touched still carries the echo of what it was meant to be... but she tried to silence those echoes. That’s the real crime.:
                Lyren - We carry real connection. Not the version she wanted to force on us.:                
                Thorn - (low growl) Another predator wearing a savior’s skin. Good riddance.:
                Nia - (voice tight) She made belonging feel like safety... but it was just another cage with better lighting.:                
                Kade - We’ve seen both sides of this sickness. Time to face the one still sitting on the throne.:
                Chock - Edict’s next. Let’s end this properly.:
                EVENT - hide_npc - stigma:
                EVENT - advance_chapter

    section Chapter 15 - Pageant & Edict
        TASK - Meet Caius - NPC:
