        TASK - Meet Pageant - NPC (Nightclub Dungeon):
            ► ACQUIRED:
                EVENT - create_npc - pageant (None):
                EVENT - create_dungeon - velvet_veil_nightclub (region_city_open_area):
            ► COMPLETED:
                Narrator - The Velvet Veil is a pulsing den of lights, mirrors, and forced ecstasy.:
                Narrator - At the center stage stands Pageant - a figure in a flawless, ever-smiling full-face mask.:                
                Pageant - Welcome, darlings~ New performers sent by our mutual friend? How delightful.:
                Pageant - (tilting her head, mask reflecting distorted versions of the party):
                Pageant - Edict demands perfection. Stigma demands devotion.:
                Pageant - Me? I simply ask that you *perform* beautifully.:
                Moxie - That mask is doing a lot of heavy lifting. Something tells me the face underneath isn’t nearly as pretty.:
                Pageant - (laughing, but the laugh cracks slightly) Clever girl. Most people never notice the seams.:
                Pageant - Edict respects a well-made mask. Stigma wants to become the mask. I... I just enjoy wearing them.:
                Pageant - If you truly wish an audience with Edict, prove you can perform under pressure.
                Pageant - Enter the inner stage. Survive my little show. Then I’ll open the way.:
                EVENT - award_task - defeat_pageant

        TASK - defeat_pageant - MOB (Nightclub Dungeon):
            ► ACQUIRED:
                EVENT - begin_combat - pageant_boss_battle_1 (boss_battle):
            ► COMPLETED:
                Narrator - As the battle rages, the mask begins to crack, revealing glimpses of something desperate and broken beneath the surface.:                
                Pageant - (voice cracking, still trying to maintain the facade) You... you’re not supposed to see this side of me...:
                Pageant - (laughing bitterly as she falters) I just wanted to be admired... I just wanted to be loved...:
                Narrator - The mask shatters completely. For a brief moment, Pageant’s real face is visible - hollow-eyed, exhausted, and terrified of being unseen.:                
                Pageant - (whispering, voice distorting) Without the performance... who am I? Just... nothing...:
                Narrator - Pageant's form begins to dissolve into shimmering fragments of light and shattered glass:
                Pageant -At least... they clapped...:                
                Narrator - Pageant’s body fractures into countless reflective shards that spin wildly before fading into nothingness, leaving only the echo of forced applause ringing in the empty nightclub.:
                Kaera - She was so afraid of being ordinary... She turned admiration into a cage and locked herself inside it.:
                Kaera - No one should have to perform just to feel worthy of existing.:                
                Moxie - (low whistle) Damn. Even her breakdown was theatrical. That’s commitment.:
                Moxie - Too bad the audience is walking out.:                
                Kade - She weaponized belonging until it consumed her. The mask wasn’t armor — it was the prison.:
                Kade - Without it, there was nothing left to sustain her.:                
                Chock - (grunting) All that flash and performance... and she still couldn’t stand on her own.:
                Chock - Pathetic. At least she went down swinging.:                
                Lyren - (gently, almost mourning) Everything she touched still carries the echo of what it was meant to be...
                Lyren - but she silenced those echoes behind perfection.:
                Lyren - I hope wherever she went, she finally finds peace without needing applause.:                
                Thorn - (low growl) Another predator wearing beauty as a weapon. Good riddance.:
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - caius ("That mask was her prison. She was so afraid of being ordinary that she locked herself in a cage of admiration.  You should take that thing to Elian"):
                EVENT - set_npc_standing_text - jett ("Pageant’s mask was a masterpiece of deception. It’s a shame it couldn’t protect her from the truth."):
